### Why `execute(Params...)` is Deprecated in API 30 (Android 11)
The `AsyncTask.execute()` method was deprecated in Android 11 (API 30) because it relied on a single background thread, leading to poor performance and potential deadlocks. Modern apps require more robust concurrency handling, and `AsyncTask` does not align with best practices for resource management, lifecycle awareness, or structured concurrency. Android now recommends using:
- `ExecutorService` for thread management.
- Kotlin Coroutines or `WorkManager` for lifecycle-aware background tasks.

---

### Alternative: Use `ExecutorService` with SSH Library (JSch)
To execute SSH commands on a Raspberry Pi in Android 11+, replace `AsyncTask` with `ExecutorService` and a modern SSH library like [JSch](http://www.jcraft.com/jsch/). Below is the updated Android implementation.

#### Android Code (Java)
```java
// Add JSch dependency to your build.gradle:
// implementation 'com.hierynomus:sshj:0.35.0' or similar

btnUp.setOnClickListener(v -> {
    String ipAddress = txtAddress.getText().toString().trim();
    if (ipAddress.isEmpty()) {
        Toast.makeText(this, "Enter Raspberry Pi IP", Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show();
        return;
    }

    // Use a single-thread executor for SSH tasks
    ExecutorService executor = Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor();
    executor.execute(() -> {
        try {
            // SSH configuration
            JSch jsch = new JSch();
            Session session = jsch.getSession("pi", ipAddress, 22); // Replace "pi" with your SSH username
            session.setPassword("raspberry"); // Avoid hardcoding credentials (see Security Notes)
            session.setConfig("StrictHostKeyChecking", "no"); // Not recommended for production
            session.connect();

            // Execute command
            ChannelExec channel = (ChannelExec) session.openChannel("exec");
            channel.setCommand("python /path/to/script.py up");
            channel.connect();

            // Read response (optional)
            InputStream response = channel.getInputStream();
            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(response));
            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                Log.d("SSH_Response", line);
            }

            // Cleanup
            channel.disconnect();
            session.disconnect();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            Log.e("SSH_Error", "Failed to execute SSH command", e);
            runOnUiThread(() -> Toast.makeText(MainActivity.this, "SSH Error", Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show());
        }
    });
});
